          deckDescription: 'The game uses a standard 52-card French-suited deck plus two distinguishable jokers known as the big and little blooper. In total there are 54 cards, and both jokers function as special trumps rather than generic wildcards.',
          suitDescription: 'There are four French suits: spades, hearts, diamonds and clubs. On each deal a trump suit is fixed by a turned-up card, and in partnership Back Alley the bloopers count as part of the trump suit hierarchy rather than their own suit.',
          rankDescription: 'In each non-trump suit the ranks run from high to low A–K–Q–J–10–9–8–7–6–5–4–3–2. In the trump suit the big blooper is highest, the little blooper is second highest, followed by the normal ace down to two as described on Pagat.',
          dealPattern: '13 through 1, 1 through 13.',
